# Frontend Rules

- Use React and TypeScript.
- Follow Next.js App Router conventions.
- Prefer Server Components when client-side interactivity is unnecessary.
- Add `"use client"` only when required.
- Use shadcn/ui components where appropriate.
- Use Tailwind CSS and existing design tokens.
- Keep components focused and reusable.
- Use Zod schemas for form validation.
- Display loading, empty, validation, and error states.
- Do not call external flight providers directly from browser components.
- Do not expose server-side API keys.
- Do not calculate authoritative flight savings in the UI.
- Keep UI display logic separate from business logic.
